From 273feb8964361226ea89866593baf11c1257c23b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:48:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop/kanban): one board across every gateway, gateway
 filter + device glyph on cards [daveey]

The Kanban page now reads the selected board from EVERY registered gateway
(local, ssh, cloud) and merges the columns; each card is tagged with its
owning gateway and shows the sidebar session row's device glyph (laptop /
Mac mini / cloud). Writes (move, edit, comment, reassign, reclaim, delete,
attachments, estimate, bulk) are routed back to the owning gateway and
board; bulk ops split per gateway; the dispatcher nudge follows the write.
New tasks go to the gateway filter's pick, else the active gateway.

- Filter menu: All gateways / one gateway (persisted), with an outage mark.
- Board switcher: union of boards across gateways, totals summed, glyphs
  for the gateways carrying each board; management actions only when the
  active gateway has the board.
- Remote reads have a hard 6s deadline (the bridge timeout does not cover a
  pending OAuth login) and a 60s cool-down; failures show as a header chip.
- Remote gateways have no events socket here: the board polls every 15s
  when more than one gateway is registered.
- SDK: PluginRestOptions.connectionId, host.state.gateways, GatewayDeviceIcon.

Single-gateway setups take the old code path unchanged.
